    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0654" n="538" xml:id="pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 888.111/69.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On May 18 the French war vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Descartes</hi> arrived
                    here and will remain pending the settlement of the Syrian question, as I am told
                    by an employee of the French Legation, which is protecting Turkish interests.
                    The Haitian Government seems determined to close, on May 31, all stores operated
                    by Syrians, Ottoman subjects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
